/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Leviticus chapters 6-10
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("leviticus", [
{n:6, name:"Laws of the Offerings",
 seal:{ref:"Leviticus 6:13",verse:"The fire shall ever be burning upon the altar; it shall never go out."},
 facts:["Did you know the fire on the altar was never allowed to go out, not even through the night? (Leviticus 6:13)","Did you know the priest changed out of his holy linen garments before carrying the ashes outside the camp? (Leviticus 6:10-11)","Did you know a guilty man had to repay what he took plus a fifth more before he ever brought his offering? (Leviticus 6:5)"],
 questions:[
  {q:"According to Leviticus 6:2, what counts as a trespass against the LORD?", options:["Lying to his neighbor about a deposit or a partnership, taking by violence, or deceiving him","Offering a sacrifice on an altar other than the tabernacle's","Eating the blood of a clean animal","Marrying within the forbidden degrees"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:2",verse:"If a soul sin, and commit a trespass against the LORD, and lie unto his neighbour in that which was delivered him to keep, or in fellowship, or in a thing taken away by violence, or hath deceived his neighbour;",
   insight:"Sin against a neighbor is counted as sin against the LORD Himself. How we treat people is never separate from how we treat God."},
  {q:"Besides restoring the full amount, what extra did the guilty person pay to the one he wronged?", options:["A fifth part more","A tenth part more","Double the whole amount","A ram from his flock"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:5",verse:"Or all that about which he hath sworn falsely; he shall even restore it in the principal, and shall add the fifth part more thereto, and give it unto him to whom it appertaineth, in the day of his trespass offering.",
   insight:"Restitution cost more than the theft. God builds the pain of the loss into repayment, so that making things right truly costs us something."},
  {q:"What animal did the guilty man bring as his trespass offering?", options:["A ram without blemish from the flock","A young calf","A turtledove","A goat of the first year"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:6",verse:"And he shall bring his trespass offering unto the LORD, a ram without blemish out of the flock, with thy estimation, for a trespass offering, unto the priest:",
   insight:"Only the best animal would do, valued by the priest's estimation. God is not honored with leftovers or damaged goods."},
  {q:"How long was the burnt offering to keep burning on the altar?", options:["All night until the morning","Until the third day","For exactly seven hours","Until the evening sacrifice only"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:9",verse:"Command Aaron and his sons, saying, This is the law of the burnt offering: It is the burnt offering, because of the burning upon the altar all night unto the morning, and the fire of the altar shall be burning in it.",
   insight:"The offering burned through the dark hours. Worship does not clock out when the day ends; God is served in the night watches too."},
  {q:"What did the priest put on when he took up the ashes from the altar?", options:["His linen garments, with linen breeches","The golden ephod and breastplate","Sackcloth over his coat","A white robe dipped in oil"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:10",verse:"And the priest shall put on his linen garment, and his linen breeches shall he put upon his flesh, and take up the ashes which the fire hath consumed with the burnt offering on the altar, and he shall put them beside the altar.",
   insight:"Even the humble work of clearing ashes was done in holy garments. No task in God's house is too low to be done with reverence."},
  {q:"Where were the ashes from the altar carried?", options:["To a clean place outside the camp","To the laver in the courtyard","Into the holy place","To the gate of the camp"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:11",verse:"And he shall put off his garments, and put on other garments, and carry forth the ashes without the camp unto a clean place.",
   insight:"The priest changed clothes first, then carried the ashes to a clean place. Order and cleanliness marked everything connected with the altar."},
  {q:"What was laid on the altar fire every morning?", options:["Wood, laid in order on the fire","Fresh incense","Olive branches","Coals from the laver"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:12",verse:"And the fire upon the altar shall be burning in it; it shall not be put out: and the priest shall burn wood on it every morning, and lay the burnt offering in order upon it; and he shall burn thereon the fat of the peace offerings.",
   insight:"The fire needed fresh wood daily. A heart that stays warm toward God needs fresh fuel every morning, not yesterday's embers."},
  {q:"What command about the altar fire is repeated twice in this chapter?", options:["It shall ever be burning on the altar; it shall never go out","It shall be quenched every Sabbath","It shall burn only at night","It shall be lit afresh each morning"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:13",verse:"The fire shall ever be burning upon the altar; it shall never go out.",
   insight:"God repeats Himself when the matter is weighty. Perpetual fire meant perpetual devotion; the flame of worship was never to die."},
  {q:"What portion of the grain offering was burned on the altar as a memorial?", options:["A handful of the fine flour, the oil, and all the frankincense","The whole offering, all of it","Only the frankincense","Half the flour and half the oil"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:15",verse:"And he shall take of it his handful, of the flour of the meat offering, and of the oil thereof, and all the frankincense which is upon the meat offering, and shall burn it upon the altar for a sweet savour, even the memorial of it, unto the LORD.",
   insight:"A handful burned, the rest given to the priests. God takes His memorial portion first, and what remains becomes provision for His servants."},
  {q:"Who ate the remainder of the grain offering, and where?", options:["Aaron and his sons, unleavened, in the holy place","The offerer and his family, at home","Only the high priest, inside the veil","The Levites, at the camp gate"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:16",verse:"And the remainder thereof shall Aaron and his sons eat: with unleavened bread shall it be eaten in the holy place; in the court of the tabernacle of the congregation they shall eat it.",
   insight:"God fed His priests from His own altar. Those who serve Him may trust Him to provide for them from His hand."},
  {q:"Why must the priests' portion of the grain offering never be baked with leaven?", options:["Because it is most holy, God's own portion of the offerings made by fire","Because leaven was too costly to waste","Because unleavened bread lasted longer in storage","Because leaven was forbidden in the whole camp"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:17",verse:"It shall not be baken with leaven. I have given it unto them for their portion of my offerings made by fire; it is most holy, as is the sin offering, and as the trespass offering.",
   insight:"Leaven pictures corruption spreading through the whole lump. What is most holy must be kept pure and unmixed."},
  {q:"Who was permitted to eat of the offerings made by fire to the LORD?", options:["Every male among the children of Aaron","Any Israelite who was clean","Only Aaron himself","Every firstborn son in Israel"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:18",verse:"All the males among the children of Aaron shall eat of it. It shall be a statute for ever in your generations concerning the offerings of the LORD made by fire: every one that toucheth them shall be holy.",
   insight:"Holiness had boundaries; not everyone could eat at this table. Nearness to God is a privilege with conditions, not an open right."},
  {q:"What was the high priest's daily grain offering, begun on the day he was anointed?", options:["The tenth part of an ephah of fine flour, half in the morning and half at night","A full ephah of wheat, once a week","A lamb every morning and evening","Two loaves of leavened bread daily"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:20",verse:"This is the offering of Aaron and of his sons, which they shall offer unto the LORD in the day when he is anointed; the tenth part of an ephah of fine flour for a meat offering perpetual, half of it in the morning, and half thereof at night.",
   insight:"The high priest's offering never stopped, morning and night. Leaders are called to a steadier rhythm of devotion than anyone."},
  {q:"How was the high priest's grain offering prepared?", options:["Baked in a pan with oil, then brought in pieces","Baked in an oven without oil","Roasted whole over the altar fire","Fried and eaten raw"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:21",verse:"In a pan it shall be made with oil; and when it is baken, thou shalt bring it in: and the baken pieces of the meat offering shalt thou offer for a sweet savour unto the LORD.",
   insight:"It was carefully prepared, piece by piece, as a sweet savor. God notices the care we put into what we bring Him."},
  {q:"Who was to keep offering this perpetual grain offering after Aaron?", options:["The priest among his sons anointed in his place","The eldest son of Judah","The Levite on duty that week","Any priest who volunteered"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:22",verse:"And the priest of his sons that is anointed in his stead shall offer it: it is a statute for ever unto the LORD, it shall be wholly burnt.",
   insight:"The office outlived the man. God's work continues through faithful successors, not through one irreplaceable person."},
  {q:"What was done with the high priest's grain offering?", options:["It was wholly burned on the altar; none of it was eaten","It was eaten by the priests like other grain offerings","It was given to the poor of the camp","It was stored in the treasury"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:23",verse:"For every meat offering for the priest shall be wholly burnt: it shall not be eaten.",
   insight:"The priest's own offering was entirely God's. Those who minister must sometimes give what they themselves cannot keep."},
  {q:"Where was the sin offering to be killed?", options:["In the place where the burnt offering is killed, before the LORD","Outside the camp with the ashes","At the door of the offerer's tent","Inside the holy place"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:25",verse:"Speak unto Aaron and to his sons, saying, This is the law of the sin offering: In the place where the burnt offering is killed shall the sin offering be killed before the LORD: it is most holy.",
   insight:"One appointed place for the shedding of blood. God fixes the meeting place; we do not get to choose our own terms of atonement."},
  {q:"What had to be done with a garment sprinkled with the blood of the sin offering?", options:["It was washed in the holy place","It was burned with the offering","It was given to the offerer as a keepsake","It was hung at the tabernacle door"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:27",verse:"Whatsoever shall touch the flesh thereof shall be holy: and when there is sprinkled of the blood thereof upon any garment, thou shalt wash that whereon it was sprinkled in the holy place.",
   insight:"The blood made whatever it touched holy. Contact with the sacrifice changed the status of common things, and still does."},
  {q:"What was done with the earthen pot in which the sin offering was boiled?", options:["It was broken; a bronze pot was scoured and rinsed in water","It was set apart for the priests' own cooking","It was washed and used again","It was buried outside the camp"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:28",verse:"But the earthen vessel wherein it is sodden shall be broken: and if it be sodden in a brasen pot, it shall be both scoured, and rinsed in water.",
   insight:"Clay absorbed what bronze could release. Some vessels, once marked by holy use, are finished with that one service."},
  {q:"Which sin offering was never to be eaten, but burned in the fire?", options:["One whose blood was carried into the tabernacle to make atonement in the holy place","One offered by a poor man with flour","One offered for a Nazarite","One whose fat was burned on the altar"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 6:30",verse:"And no sin offering, whereof any of the blood is brought into the tabernacle of the congregation to reconcile withal in the holy place, shall be eaten: it shall be burnt in the fire.",
   insight:"The deeper the blood went, the more complete the burning. The most solemn atonements left nothing for man to keep."}
 ]},
{n:7, name:"The Guilt Offering and the Priests' Portion",
 seal:{ref:"Leviticus 7:37",verse:"This is the law of the burnt offering, of the meat offering, and of the sin offering, and of the trespass offering, and of the consecrations, and of the sacrifice of the peace offerings;"},
 facts:["Did you know the peace offering was the one sacrifice the worshiper himself ate, sharing a fellowship meal in God's presence? (Leviticus 7:15)","Did you know the priest's share, the breast and the right shoulder, was lifted up and waved before the LORD before he received it? (Leviticus 7:30)","Did you know Leviticus 7 closes by naming all the offerings together in one summary of the laws given at Sinai? (Leviticus 7:37)"],
 questions:[
  {q:"How does Leviticus 7 describe the trespass offering?", options:["It is most holy","It is the lightest of the offerings","It is offered only at Passover","It is eaten by the whole congregation"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:1",verse:"Likewise this is the law of the trespass offering: it is most holy.",
   insight:"Guilt before God is a weighty matter, not a light one. Calling the offering most holy teaches us to take our wrongs seriously."},
  {q:"Where was the trespass offering killed?", options:["In the place where the burnt offering is killed","On the Mount of Olives","At the Jordan river","Before the ark inside the veil"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:2",verse:"In the place where they kill the burnt offering shall they kill the trespass offering: and the blood thereof shall he sprinkle round about upon the altar.",
   insight:"Every offering had its appointed ground. God decides where atonement happens; we come to His place, not our own."},
  {q:"Which parts of the trespass offering were burned on the altar?", options:["The fat, the whole rump, the kidneys, and the caul above the liver","The head and the legs","The blood and the hide","The shoulders and the breast"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:3",verse:"And he shall offer of it all the fat thereof; the rump, and the fat that covereth the inwards,",
   insight:"The richest parts belonged to God. The fat was the best of the animal, and the best of everything still belongs to Him."},
  {q:"Who was to eat the trespass offering, and where?", options:["Every male among the priests, in the holy place","The offerer with his household, at home","The elders of Israel, at the tabernacle door","Only the high priest, inside the veil"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:6",verse:"Every male among the priests shall eat thereof: it shall be eaten in the holy place: it is most holy.",
   insight:"The priests ate what had carried another's guilt. Bearing the burden of sin was their calling, and God sustained them in it."},
  {q:"What part of the burnt offering belonged to the priest who offered it?", options:["The skin of the burnt offering","The right shoulder","The breast","The fat"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:8",verse:"And the priest that offereth any man’s burnt offering, even the priest shall have to himself the skin of the burnt offering which he hath offered.",
   insight:"Even when the whole animal went up in flame, God remembered His servant. Faithful service is never left unprovided for."},
  {q:"To whom did a grain offering baked in the oven belong?", options:["The priest who offered it","The offerer","The Levites","The whole priesthood in common"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:9",verse:"And all the meat offering that is baken in the oven, and all that is dressed in the fryingpan, and in the pan, shall be the priest’s that offereth it.",
   insight:"The laborer is worthy of his hire. God ties the priest's provision directly to the ministry he performs."},
  {q:"How was an uncooked grain offering shared among the priests?", options:["Equally, to all the sons of Aaron alike","Given entirely to the high priest","Divided by lot each month","Sold for the treasury"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:10",verse:"And every meat offering, mingled with oil, and dry, shall all the sons of Aaron have, one as much as another.",
   insight:"One as much as another. Among God's servants there is no jostling for the larger share; He portions it out evenly."},
  {q:"What bread was offered with a peace offering given for thanksgiving?", options:["Unleavened cakes mingled with oil, wafers anointed with oil, and fried cakes of fine flour","Twelve loaves of leavened bread","Seven barley loaves","Only a single wafer"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:12",verse:"If he offer it for a thanksgiving, then he shall offer with the sacrifice of thanksgiving unleavened cakes mingled with oil, and unleavened wafers anointed with oil, and cakes mingled with oil, of fine flour, fried.",
   insight:"Thanksgiving came with abundance and variety. A grateful heart does not bring God the bare minimum."},
  {q:"What kind of bread was also added to the thanksgiving offering?", options:["Leavened bread","Bread made with honey","Bread baked in ashes","No other bread at all"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:13",verse:"Besides the cakes, he shall offer for his offering leavened bread with the sacrifice of thanksgiving of his peace offerings.",
   insight:"Here leaven was allowed, unlike other offerings. God makes room for the honest imperfection of a thankful, ordinary worshiper."},
  {q:"What was done with one cake out of the whole thanksgiving offering?", options:["It was given to the priest who sprinkled the blood, as a heave offering to the LORD","It was burned whole on the altar","It was cast into the fire outside","It was eaten by the offerer's children"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:14",verse:"And of it he shall offer one out of the whole oblation for an heave offering unto the LORD, and it shall be the priest’s that sprinkleth the blood of the peace offerings.",
   insight:"One cake lifted up to God before the meal began. Thanksgiving starts by setting the first portion aside for Him."},
  {q:"By when did the flesh of the thanksgiving offering have to be eaten?", options:["The same day it was offered; none was to remain until morning","Within seven days","Before the next Sabbath","Within three days"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:15",verse:"And the flesh of the sacrifice of his peace offerings for thanksgiving shall be eaten the same day that it is offered; he shall not leave any of it until the morning.",
   insight:"Thanksgiving could not be postponed or stored. Gratitude is a present-tense offering; delayed thanks loses its savor."},
  {q:"How long could the flesh of a vow or voluntary peace offering be eaten?", options:["The day it was offered and the next day; what remained on the third day was burned","Only on the day it was offered","For a full week","Until the new moon"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:16",verse:"But if the sacrifice of his offering be a vow, or a voluntary offering, it shall be eaten the same day that he offereth his sacrifice: and on the morrow also the remainder of it shall be eaten:",
   insight:"God sets a shelf life on our devotions. Some gifts are meant to be enjoyed promptly, not hoarded for later."},
  {q:"What happened if the peace offering was eaten on the third day?", options:["It was not accepted, it was an abomination, and the eater bore his iniquity","The eater was fined a shekel","The offering was offered again","Nothing; it was still acceptable"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:18",verse:"And if any of the flesh of the sacrifice of his peace offerings be eaten at all on the third day, it shall not be accepted, neither shall it be imputed unto him that offereth it: it shall be an abomination, and the soul that eateth of it shall bear his iniquity.",
   insight:"Late obedience spoiled into disobedience. Worship done on our own schedule, past God's limit, becomes an abomination."},
  {q:"What was done with sacrificial flesh that touched anything unclean?", options:["It was not eaten but burned with fire","It was washed and then eaten","It was given to the dogs","It was buried under the altar"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:19",verse:"And the flesh that toucheth any unclean thing shall not be eaten; it shall be burnt with fire: and as for the flesh, all that be clean shall eat thereof.",
   insight:"Holiness is contagious in the wrong direction too; contact with uncleanness ruined the holy. Guard what is sacred from careless contact."},
  {q:"Who was cut off from his people for eating the peace offering?", options:["The one who ate its flesh while he himself was unclean","The one who ate it too slowly","The one who shared it with a stranger","The one who cooked it at home"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:20",verse:"But the soul that eateth of the flesh of the sacrifice of peace offerings, that pertain unto the LORD, having his uncleanness upon him, even that soul shall be cut off from his people.",
   insight:"Coming to God's table in an unclean state was a grave offense. Fellowship with God requires a clean heart, not just an appetite."},
  {q:"What else brought the same judgment on one who ate of the peace offering?", options:["Touching the uncleanness of man, an unclean beast, or any abominable unclean thing","Touching the altar with bare hands","Wearing torn garments","Speaking during the sacrifice"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:21",verse:"Moreover the soul that shall touch any unclean thing, as the uncleanness of man, or any unclean beast, or any abominable unclean thing, and eat of the flesh of the sacrifice of peace offerings, which pertain unto the LORD, even that soul shall be cut off from his people.",
   insight:"Defilement came through contact, and contact was a choice. Wisdom watches what we touch, not only what we intend."},
  {q:"Whose fat was Israel forbidden to eat?", options:["The fat of ox, of sheep, and of goat","The fat of fish and birds","The fat of deer and gazelle","All fat of every kind"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:23",verse:"Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, Ye shall eat no manner of fat, of ox, or of sheep, or of goat.",
   insight:"The best portion was reserved for God alone. Some things are not ours to consume, no matter how good they look."},
  {q:"What could be done with the fat of an animal that died on its own?", options:["It could be used for any other purpose, but it must not be eaten","Nothing; it had to be burned at once","It could be sold to foreigners only","It was given to the priests to eat"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:24",verse:"And the fat of the beast that dieth of itself, and the fat of that which is torn with beasts, may be used in any other use: but ye shall in no wise eat of it.",
   insight:"God distinguishes use from consumption. Not every restriction is absolute; wisdom learns which lines are firm and which allow freedom."},
  {q:"What was the penalty for eating blood?", options:["That soul was cut off from his people","A trespass offering of a ram","Seven days outside the camp","Forty stripes"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:26",verse:"Moreover ye shall eat no manner of blood, whether it be of fowl or of beast, in any of your dwellings.",
   insight:"The blood was the life, and the life belonged to God. Treating lightly what God calls sacred carries the heaviest cost."},
  {q:"Which parts of the peace offering belonged to the priests?", options:["The wave breast to Aaron and his sons, and the right shoulder to the priest who offered the blood and the fat","The whole animal except the fat","Only the hide and the horns","The loins and the neck"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 7:31",verse:"And the priest shall burn the fat upon the altar: but the breast shall be Aaron’s and his sons’.",
   insight:"The breast near the heart and the shoulder of strength. God honors His servants with portions that speak of love and labor."}
 ]},
{n:8, name:"The Consecration of Aaron",
 seal:{ref:"Leviticus 8:36",verse:"So Aaron and his sons did all things which the LORD commanded by the hand of Moses."},
 facts:["Did you know Moses put blood on Aaron's right ear, right thumb, and right big toe, marking his hearing, his work, and his walk as holy? (Leviticus 8:23-24)","Did you know Moses, though not a priest, received the breast of the ram of consecration as his own portion? (Leviticus 8:29)","Did you know the ordination lasted seven full days, during which Aaron and his sons could not leave the tabernacle door? (Leviticus 8:33)"],
 questions:[
  {q:"What did the LORD tell Moses to gather for the consecration?", options:["Aaron and his sons, the garments, the anointing oil, a bullock for the sin offering, two rams, and a basket of unleavened bread","Twelve oxen and the ark of the covenant","Gold, silver, and precious stones","The elders and the book of the law"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:2",verse:"Take Aaron and his sons with him, and the garments, and the anointing oil, and a bullock for the sin offering, and two rams, and a basket of unleavened bread;",
   insight:"God listed everything needed before the ceremony began. Preparation is part of obedience; consecration is never improvised."},
  {q:"Where did the whole congregation assemble for the consecration?", options:["At the door of the tabernacle of the congregation","At the foot of Mount Sinai","Inside the holy place","Around the bronze altar only"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:3",verse:"And gather thou all the congregation together unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.",
   insight:"The whole nation watched their priests set apart. Leadership is consecrated in public, because it will be exercised in public."},
  {q:"What was the first thing Moses did to Aaron and his sons?", options:["He washed them with water","He anointed their heads with oil","He clothed them in the holy garments","He sprinkled them with blood"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:6",verse:"And Moses brought Aaron and his sons, and washed them with water.",
   insight:"Washing came before clothing. Cleansing precedes service; God washes those He calls before He dresses them for the work."},
  {q:"What did Moses put inside Aaron's breastplate?", options:["The Urim and the Thummim","The two stone tablets","Twelve precious stones for the tribes","A scroll of the law"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:8",verse:"And he put the breastplate upon him: also he put in the breastplate the Urim and the Thummim.",
   insight:"The means of discerning God's will rested over Aaron's heart. Leaders need guidance close to the heart, not just duties on the hands."},
  {q:"What was fastened to the front of Aaron's mitre?", options:["The golden plate, the holy crown","A blue lace rosette","A silver trumpet","The Urim and Thummim"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:9",verse:"And he put the mitre upon his head; also upon the mitre, even upon his forefront, did he put the golden plate, the holy crown; as the LORD commanded Moses.",
   insight:"Holiness to the LORD shone on his forehead for all to see. A consecrated mind is the most visible mark of God's servant."},
  {q:"Besides Aaron, what did Moses anoint with the oil?", options:["The tabernacle and all in it, the altar and its vessels, and the laver","The twelve tribes' standards","The ark only","The camp of Israel"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:10",verse:"And Moses took the anointing oil, and anointed the tabernacle and all that was therein, and sanctified them.",
   insight:"The place and the tools were anointed as well as the man. Everything that touches God's work shares in its consecration."},
  {q:"How did Moses anoint Aaron himself?", options:["He poured the anointing oil upon Aaron's head","He sprinkled a few drops on his hands","He dipped Aaron's finger in oil","He anointed only his garments"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:12",verse:"And he poured of the anointing oil upon Aaron’s head, and anointed him, to sanctify him.",
   insight:"The oil was poured, not dabbed. God's anointing is abundant, running down; He does not measure out His Spirit sparingly."},
  {q:"What was the bullock brought for at the consecration?", options:["A sin offering","A peace offering","A burnt offering","A thank offering"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:14",verse:"And he brought the bullock for the sin offering: and Aaron and his sons laid their hands upon the head of the bullock for the sin offering.",
   insight:"Even the new priests began with a sin offering. No one is consecrated for holy work without first dealing with sin."},
  {q:"What did Moses do with the blood of the sin offering bullock?", options:["He put it on the horns of the altar with his finger and poured the rest at the bottom of the altar","He sprinkled it seven times inside the veil","He poured it into the laver","He carried it around the camp"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:15",verse:"And he slew it; and Moses took the blood, and put it upon the horns of the altar round about with his finger, and purified the altar, and poured the blood at the bottom of the altar, and sanctified it, to make reconciliation upon it.",
   insight:"The altar itself had to be cleansed and sanctified. The instruments of worship need atonement as much as the worshipers."},
  {q:"What was the first ram offered as?", options:["A burnt offering","A peace offering","A trespass offering","A wave offering"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:18",verse:"And he brought the ram for the burnt offering: and Aaron and his sons laid their hands upon the head of the ram.",
   insight:"Total surrender followed cleansing. The burnt offering, wholly consumed, pictures a life given to God without remainder."},
  {q:"What parts of the burnt offering ram were washed in water before it was burned?", options:["The inwards and the legs","The head and the fat","The hide and the horns","The breast and the shoulder"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:21",verse:"And he washed the inwards and the legs in water; and Moses burnt the whole ram upon the altar: it was a burnt sacrifice for a sweet savour, and an offering made by fire unto the LORD; as the LORD commanded Moses.",
   insight:"The inward parts were washed clean. God looks past the outward presentation to the inward condition of what we offer."},
  {q:"What was the second ram called?", options:["The ram of consecration","The ram of atonement","The ram of the covenant","The ram of thanksgiving"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:22",verse:"And he brought the other ram, the ram of consecration: and Aaron and his sons laid their hands upon the head of the ram.",
   insight:"This ram belonged to the setting-apart itself. Consecration has its own sacrifice; being set apart costs something specific."},
  {q:"Where did Moses put the blood of the ram of consecration on Aaron?", options:["On the tip of his right ear, the thumb of his right hand, and the great toe of his right foot","On his forehead, his lips, and his heart","On his shoulders and his back","On his garments only"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:23",verse:"And he slew it; and Moses took of the blood of it, and put it upon the tip of Aaron’s right ear, and upon the thumb of his right hand, and upon the great toe of his right foot.",
   insight:"Ear, hand, and foot: what he hears, what he does, where he goes. Consecration touches the whole life, not just the religious hours."},
  {q:"What was laid on the fat and the right shoulder before they were waved?", options:["One unleavened cake, one cake of oiled bread, and one wafer","Three loaves of leavened bread","A bowl of oil and wine","Seven ears of corn"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:26",verse:"And out of the basket of unleavened bread, that was before the LORD, he took one unleavened cake, and a cake of oiled bread, and one wafer, and put them on the fat, and upon the right shoulder:",
   insight:"Bread joined the sacrifice in the priests' hands. Worship and daily provision meet in the same offering."},
  {q:"What was done with the cakes, the fat, and the right shoulder?", options:["They were placed in the priests' hands and waved as a wave offering before the LORD","They were burned at once on the altar","They were eaten by Moses","They were buried outside the camp"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:27",verse:"And he put all upon Aaron’s hands, and upon his sons’ hands, and waved them for a wave offering before the LORD.",
   insight:"The priests held the offering in their own hands and waved it to God. Consecration is personal; it must pass through your own hands."},
  {q:"Which part of the ram of consecration belonged to Moses?", options:["The breast, which he waved as a wave offering","The right shoulder","The kidneys and the fat","The whole ram"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:29",verse:"And Moses took the breast, and waved it for a wave offering before the LORD: for of the ram of consecration it was Moses’ part; as the LORD commanded Moses.",
   insight:"The mediator received his portion too. God provides for those who stand between Him and the people in faithful service."},
  {q:"With what were Aaron, his sons, and their garments sprinkled to sanctify them?", options:["The anointing oil and the blood from the altar","Water from the laver only","Oil and wine mixed","The ashes of the burnt offering"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:30",verse:"And Moses took of the anointing oil, and of the blood which was upon the altar, and sprinkled it upon Aaron, and upon his garments, and upon his sons, and upon his sons’ garments with him; and sanctified Aaron, and his garments, and his sons, and his sons’ garments with him.",
   insight:"Oil and blood together: the Spirit and the sacrifice. Both mark the consecrated life; neither alone is enough."},
  {q:"Where did Aaron and his sons eat the consecration meal?", options:["At the door of the tabernacle of the congregation","Inside the holy of holies","In Aaron's tent","At the foot of the mountain"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:31",verse:"And Moses said unto Aaron and to his sons, Boil the flesh at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation: and there eat it with the bread that is in the basket of consecrations, as I commanded, saying, Aaron and his sons shall eat it.",
   insight:"They ate at the doorway, between God and the people. The priest's place is at the threshold, belonging to both and set apart from both."},
  {q:"How long were Aaron and his sons to remain at the tabernacle door?", options:["Seven days, until the days of their consecration were ended","Forty days and forty nights","Three days","One full year"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:33",verse:"And ye shall not go out of the door of the tabernacle of the congregation in seven days, until the days of your consecration be at an end: for seven days shall he consecrate you.",
   insight:"Consecration took a full week of staying put. Becoming holy is not instant; it requires remaining where God placed you."},
  {q:"What were the priests commanded to do day and night during those seven days?", options:["Keep the charge of the LORD, that they might not die","Offer a new sacrifice every hour","Read the law aloud to the people","Fast from bread and water"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 8:35",verse:"Therefore shall ye abide at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation day and night seven days, and keep the charge of the LORD, that ye die not: for so I am commanded.",
   insight:"Their whole duty was to keep charge, to watch and wait. Sometimes obedience is simply staying at your post, day and night."}
 ]},
{n:9, name:"The Priests Begin Their Ministry",
 seal:{ref:"Leviticus 9:24",verse:"And there came a fire out from before the LORD, and consumed upon the altar the burnt offering and the fat: which when all the people saw, they shouted, and fell on their faces."},
 facts:["Did you know fire fell from the LORD and consumed the offering on the very first day Aaron ministered as high priest? (Leviticus 9:24)","Did you know Aaron had to offer a sin offering for himself before he could offer for the people? (Leviticus 9:7)","Did you know Moses and Aaron blessed the people together, and then the glory of the LORD appeared to everyone? (Leviticus 9:23)"],
 questions:[
  {q:"On which day did Aaron begin his priestly ministry?", options:["On the eighth day","On the seventh day","On the first day of the month","On the Day of Atonement"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:1",verse:"And it came to pass on the eighth day, that Moses called Aaron and his sons, and the elders of Israel;",
   insight:"Seven days of consecration, then the eighth day of beginning. New work starts after the preparation is complete, not before."},
  {q:"What was Aaron himself to bring for his own sin offering?", options:["A young calf without blemish","A full-grown bull","A lamb of the first year","Two turtledoves"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:2",verse:"And he said unto Aaron, Take thee a young calf for a sin offering, and a ram for a burnt offering, without blemish, and offer them before the LORD.",
   insight:"The high priest was not exempt from his own sin. Those who lead others to God must first deal with their own guilt."},
  {q:"What did the children of Israel bring for their sin offering that day?", options:["A kid of the goats","A young calf","A red heifer","A ram"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:3",verse:"And unto the children of Israel thou shalt speak, saying, Take ye a kid of the goats for a sin offering; and a calf and a lamb, both of the first year, without blemish, for a burnt offering;",
   insight:"The people brought their own offering too. No one rides on the priest's sacrifice; every soul comes to God for itself."},
  {q:"Why were all these offerings commanded on that particular day?", options:["Because the LORD would appear to them that day","Because it was the Passover","Because the tabernacle was finished","Because Moses was leaving"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:4",verse:"Also a bullock and a ram for peace offerings, to sacrifice before the LORD; and a meat offering mingled with oil: for to day the LORD will appear unto you.",
   insight:"Sacrifice prepared the way for God's appearing. We prepare for God's presence through atonement, not through performance."},
  {q:"What did Moses say would happen if they did what the LORD commanded?", options:["The glory of the LORD would appear to them","Their enemies would be defeated","It would rain in the wilderness","They would enter Canaan that year"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:6",verse:"And Moses said, This is the thing which the LORD commanded that ye should do: and the glory of the LORD shall appear unto you.",
   insight:"Obedience opens the way to glory. God attaches His presence to simple compliance with what He has said."},
  {q:"What did Moses command Aaron to do before offering for the people?", options:["Offer the sin offering and burnt offering for himself first, making atonement for himself and the people","Wash the people with water","Bless the people from the altar","Light the lamps in the holy place"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:7",verse:"And Moses said unto Aaron, Go unto the altar, and offer thy sin offering, and thy burnt offering, and make an atonement for thyself, and for the people: and offer the offering of the people, and make an atonement for them; as the LORD commanded.",
   insight:"Atonement for himself came first. A minister cannot lead others where he has not gone himself."},
  {q:"What did Aaron do with the blood of his sin offering calf?", options:["He dipped his finger in it, put it on the horns of the altar, and poured the rest at the altar's base","He sprinkled it toward the veil seven times","He poured it into the laver","He carried it around the camp"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:9",verse:"And the sons of Aaron brought the blood unto him: and he dipped his finger in the blood, and put it upon the horns of the altar, and poured out the blood at the bottom of the altar:",
   insight:"The horns, the place of power, received the blood first. Atonement touches the strongest points of our defense before anything else."},
  {q:"What happened to the flesh and hide of Aaron's sin offering?", options:["They were burned with fire outside the camp","They were eaten by the priests","They were given to the offerer","They were buried under the altar"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:11",verse:"And the flesh and the hide he burnt with fire without the camp.",
   insight:"The sin bearer was carried outside, away from the camp. Sin is not kept close; it is removed to a distance."},
  {q:"How was Aaron's burnt offering presented to him?", options:["His sons delivered it to him piece by piece, along with the head","It was lifted whole onto the altar","It was cut in two only","It was burned without being cut"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:13",verse:"And they presented the burnt offering unto him, with the pieces thereof, and the head: and he burnt them upon the altar.",
   insight:"Ministry is shared work; his sons brought the pieces. Even the high priest needed others serving alongside him."},
  {q:"What did Aaron wash before burning the burnt offering?", options:["The inwards and the legs","The hide and the horns","The blood and the fat","The head only"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:14",verse:"And he did wash the inwards and the legs, and burnt them upon the burnt offering on the altar.",
   insight:"Again the inward parts were washed. God keeps returning to the inside, because that is where He looks."},
  {q:"What did Aaron offer as the people's sin offering?", options:["A goat, offered in the same manner as his own","A second calf","Two lambs","A bullock"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:15",verse:"And he brought the people’s offering, and took the goat, which was the sin offering for the people, and slew it, and offered it for sin, as the first.",
   insight:"As the first, so the second: the people's offering followed the same pattern. There is one way of atonement for priest and people alike."},
  {q:"How was the people's burnt offering presented?", options:["According to the prescribed manner","Without any blood ritual","Outside the camp","By the elders, not Aaron"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:16",verse:"And he brought the burnt offering, and offered it according to the manner.",
   insight:"According to the manner, no shortcuts. God's prescribed way does not change when the crowd gets larger."},
  {q:"What did Aaron do with the grain offering that day?", options:["He took a handful and burned it on the altar, besides the morning burnt offering","He ate it all himself","He gave it to the elders","He stored it in the tabernacle"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:17",verse:"And he brought the meat offering, and took an handful thereof, and burnt it upon the altar, beside the burnt sacrifice of the morning.",
   insight:"The daily rhythm continued beside the special offerings. Extraordinary days do not cancel ordinary faithfulness."},
  {q:"What animals did Aaron offer as peace offerings for the people?", options:["A bullock and a ram","Two goats","A lamb and a calf","Two rams"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:18",verse:"He slew also the bullock and the ram for a sacrifice of peace offerings, which was for the people: and Aaron’s sons presented unto him the blood, which he sprinkled upon the altar round about,",
   insight:"The peace offering sealed the day with fellowship. Atonement ends in communion; the goal was always a shared meal with God."},
  {q:"Where was the fat of the peace offerings placed before it was burned?", options:["Upon the breasts, then burned on the altar","Under the altar","On the horns","Beside the laver"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:20",verse:"And they put the fat upon the breasts, and he burnt the fat upon the altar:",
   insight:"The best was lifted up before it was given. What we return to God should first be presented to Him with honor."},
  {q:"What did Aaron wave before the LORD as Moses commanded?", options:["The breasts and the right shoulder","The whole bullock","The blood in a basin","The grain offering"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:21",verse:"And the breasts and the right shoulder Aaron waved for a wave offering before the LORD; as Moses commanded.",
   insight:"The wave offering moved toward God and back to the priest. Worship is a motion: we lift to Him, and He gives back to us."},
  {q:"What did Aaron do when he came down from offering?", options:["He lifted his hands toward the people and blessed them","He washed his hands and feet","He changed his garments at once","He counted the offerings"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:22",verse:"And Aaron lifted up his hand toward the people, and blessed them, and came down from offering of the sin offering, and the burnt offering, and peace offerings.",
   insight:"The work ended in blessing, with lifted hands. Ministry that begins at the altar should end in blessing the people."},
  {q:"What happened after Moses and Aaron came out of the tabernacle?", options:["They blessed the people, and the glory of the LORD appeared to all the people","A cloud covered the camp","The people offered their own sacrifices","Moses read the law aloud"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:23",verse:"And Moses and Aaron went into the tabernacle of the congregation, and came out, and blessed the people: and the glory of the LORD appeared unto all the people.",
   insight:"Obedience done, blessing given, glory appeared. God's presence follows the path of His commanded order."},
  {q:"What happened when fire came out from before the LORD?", options:["It consumed the burnt offering and the fat, and the people shouted and fell on their faces","A voice spoke from the cloud","The altar shook and split","Manna fell around the camp"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:24",verse:"And there came a fire out from before the LORD, and consumed upon the altar the burnt offering and the fat: which when all the people saw, they shouted, and fell on their faces.",
   insight:"God answered with fire, the seal of His approval, and the people answered with shouts and bowed faces. True worship holds reverence and rejoicing in the same moment."},
  {q:"What parts of Aaron's sin offering calf were burned on the altar?", options:["The fat, the kidneys, and the caul above the liver","The flesh and the hide","The head and the legs","The whole calf, entirely"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 9:10",verse:"But the fat, and the kidneys, and the caul above the liver of the sin offering, he burnt upon the altar; as the LORD commanded Moses.",
   insight:"The richest parts went up to God while the rest was carried outside. The best of the offering belongs on the altar, not kept back."}
 ]},
{n:10, name:"Nadab and Abihu",
 seal:{ref:"Leviticus 10:3",verse:"Then Moses said unto Aaron, This is it that the LORD spake, saying, I will be sanctified in them that come nigh me, and before all the people I will be glorified. And Aaron held his peace."},
 facts:["Did you know Nadab and Abihu died on the very first day of their priestly ministry, right after the consecration week ended? (Leviticus 10:1-2)","Did you know that in this same chapter God commanded the priests never to drink wine or strong drink when entering the tabernacle? (Leviticus 10:9)","Did you know Aaron's quiet grief moved Moses to accept his sons' burning of the sin offering instead of eating it? (Leviticus 10:19-20)"],
 questions:[
  {q:"What did Nadab and Abihu do wrong?", options:["They offered strange fire before the LORD, which He had not commanded","They refused to offer any sacrifice","They entered the holy of holies","They stole from the offerings"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:1",verse:"And Nadab and Abihu, the sons of Aaron, took either of them his censer, and put fire therein, and put incense thereon, and offered strange fire before the LORD, which he commanded them not.",
   insight:"Their sin was not refusing to worship but worshiping their own way. Zeal without obedience is still disobedience."},
  {q:"What made their fire 'strange'?", options:["It was fire the LORD had not commanded","It was blue instead of red","It was kindled on the Sabbath","It came from outside the camp"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:1",verse:"And Nadab and Abihu, the sons of Aaron, took either of them his censer, and put fire therein, and put incense thereon, and offered strange fire before the LORD, which he commanded them not.",
   insight:"Strange fire was unauthorized fire. God cares not only that we worship, but that we worship as He commands."},
  {q:"What was the immediate judgment on Nadab and Abihu?", options:["Fire went out from the LORD and devoured them, and they died before Him","They were struck with leprosy","They were exiled from the camp","They were demoted from the priesthood"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:2",verse:"And there went out fire from the LORD, and devoured them, and they died before the LORD.",
   insight:"The same fire that accepted the offering consumed the disobedient priests. God's holiness both receives and judges."},
  {q:"What reason did Moses give Aaron for this judgment, and how did Aaron respond?", options:["God said He would be sanctified in those who come near Him, and glorified before all the people; Aaron held his peace","God was angry that day for no reason; Aaron wept aloud","The people had complained about them; Aaron protested","Moses had warned them three times; Aaron tore his garments"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:3",verse:"Then Moses said unto Aaron, This is it that the LORD spake, saying, I will be sanctified in them that come nigh me, and before all the people I will be glorified. And Aaron held his peace.",
   insight:"Those nearest to God are held to the highest standard, and Aaron answered with silence. Sometimes the holiest response to God's judgment is quiet submission."},
  {q:"Who was called to carry the bodies out of the camp?", options:["Mishael and Elzaphan, the sons of Uzziel, Aaron's uncle","Eleazar and Ithamar","The seventy elders","The Levites on duty"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:4",verse:"And Moses called Mishael and Elzaphan, the sons of Uzziel the uncle of Aaron, and said unto them, Come near, carry your brethren from before the sanctuary out of the camp.",
   insight:"Aaron's own sons could not touch the dead, so cousins carried them out. Holiness sometimes requires others to do what we cannot."},
  {q:"In what were Nadab and Abihu carried out?", options:["In their coats","In linen shrouds","On a wooden bier","In sacks of ashes"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:5",verse:"So they went near, and carried them in their coats out of the camp; as Moses had said.",
   insight:"They were carried out in the very garments of their office. The robes of ministry did not shield them from judgment."},
  {q:"What mourning customs were Aaron, Eleazar, and Ithamar forbidden?", options:["They must not uncover their heads nor tear their garments, lest they die","They must not weep at all","They must not eat for seven days","They must not speak to anyone"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:6",verse:"And Moses said unto Aaron, and unto Eleazar and unto Ithamar, his sons, Uncover not your heads, neither rend your clothes; lest ye die, and lest wrath come upon all the people: but let your brethren, the whole house of Israel, bewail the burning which the LORD hath kindled.",
   insight:"Even grief had limits for the anointed. Their consecration to God outweighed their right to mourn as other men mourned."},
  {q:"Who was to mourn the burning that the LORD had kindled?", options:["The whole house of Israel","Only the priests","Only Aaron's family","No one at all"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:6",verse:"And Moses said unto Aaron, and unto Eleazar and unto Ithamar, his sons, Uncover not your heads, neither rend your clothes; lest ye die, and lest wrath come upon all the people: but let your brethren, the whole house of Israel, bewail the burning which the LORD hath kindled.",
   insight:"The nation mourned what the family could not. The whole community felt the loss, reminding Israel that holiness is everyone's concern."},
  {q:"Why could Aaron and his sons not leave the tabernacle door even to mourn?", options:["Because the anointing oil of the LORD was upon them","Because the glory had departed","Because Moses locked the door","Because the sacrifices were not finished"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:7",verse:"And ye shall not go out from the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, lest ye die: for the anointing oil of the LORD is upon you. And they did according to the word of Moses.",
   insight:"The anointing set them apart from ordinary responses. Being marked by God means some natural freedoms are laid down."},
  {q:"To whom did the LORD speak directly after these events?", options:["To Aaron","To Moses","To Eleazar","To the whole congregation"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:8",verse:"And the LORD spake unto Aaron, saying,",
   insight:"God spoke to Aaron himself, not through Moses. In the midst of loss, God drew near to the grieving father with His own voice."},
  {q:"What did the LORD forbid Aaron and his sons when they went into the tabernacle?", options:["Wine and strong drink","Bread and oil","Meat and honey","Water from the laver"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:9",verse:"Do not drink wine nor strong drink, thou, nor thy sons with thee, when ye go into the tabernacle of the congregation, lest ye die: it shall be a statute for ever throughout your generations:",
   insight:"Clear heads were required in God's presence. Anything that clouds judgment has no place in holy service."},
  {q:"Why must the priests keep clear heads in God's service?", options:["To distinguish between the holy and the unholy, and between the unclean and the clean","To set an example of fasting","To avoid quarrels among priests","To keep the wine for the offerings"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:10",verse:"And that ye may put difference between holy and unholy, and between unclean and clean;",
   insight:"Discernment is the priest's core skill: telling holy from common. That judgment fails when the mind is dulled."},
  {q:"What teaching duty did the LORD lay on the priests?", options:["To teach the children of Israel all the statutes the LORD had spoken","To teach them to read and write","To teach them farming in Canaan","To teach them the songs of Moses"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:11",verse:"And that ye may teach the children of Israel all the statutes which the LORD hath spoken unto them by the hand of Moses.",
   insight:"Priests were teachers, not just ritual workers. Those who serve God must also instruct others in His ways."},
  {q:"What did Moses tell Aaron and his remaining sons to eat after the tragedy?", options:["The remainder of the grain offering, unleavened, beside the altar, for it is most holy","The peace offerings of the people","The showbread from the table","Nothing until the next morning"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:12",verse:"And Moses spake unto Aaron, and unto Eleazar and unto Ithamar, his sons that were left, Take the meat offering that remaineth of the offerings of the LORD made by fire, and eat it without leaven beside the altar: for it is most holy:",
   insight:"Life and duty continued even in grief. God's provision waited at the altar, and the work of the LORD did not pause."},
  {q:"Where could the wave breast and heave shoulder be eaten, and by whom?", options:["In a clean place, by Aaron and his sons and his daughters","In the holy place, by the priests only","Outside the camp, by the Levites","At home, by the whole tribe"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:14",verse:"And the wave breast and heave shoulder shall ye eat in a clean place; thou, and thy sons, and thy daughters with thee: for they be thy due, and thy sons’ due, which are given out of the sacrifices of peace offerings of the children of Israel.",
   insight:"The priests' families shared in the holy portions. God's provision for His servants extends to their households."},
  {q:"What did Moses find when he diligently sought the goat of the sin offering?", options:["It had been burned up, and he was angry with Eleazar and Ithamar","It had been eaten by the people","It had escaped into the wilderness","It had never been offered"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:16",verse:"And Moses diligently sought the goat of the sin offering, and, behold, it was burnt: and he was angry with Eleazar and Ithamar, the sons of Aaron which were left alive, saying,",
   insight:"Moses checked diligently; leaders inspect what they command. Careful oversight caught the irregularity the same day."},
  {q:"What was Moses' complaint against Eleazar and Ithamar?", options:["They had not eaten the sin offering in the holy place, though God had given it to them to bear the people's iniquity","They had eaten it outside the camp","They had offered it without blood","They had refused to wave the breast"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:17",verse:"Wherefore have ye not eaten the sin offering in the holy place, seeing it is most holy, and God hath given it you to bear the iniquity of the congregation, to make atonement for them before the LORD?",
   insight:"Eating the offering was how the priests bore the people's iniquity. Skipping the duty meant the burden went uncarried."},
  {q:"Why did the law require the priests to eat that sin offering?", options:["Because its blood had not been brought inside the holy place","Because it was the Sabbath","Because the people were hungry","Because Aaron commanded it"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:18",verse:"Behold, the blood of it was not brought in within the holy place: ye should indeed have eaten it in the holy place, as I commanded.",
   insight:"The ritual had a precise logic: blood inside meant burning outside, blood outside meant eating inside. God's order leaves no room for guessing."},
  {q:"How did Aaron answer Moses?", options:["He said that after such a calamity had befallen him that day, eating the sin offering might not have been accepted by the LORD","He blamed Eleazar and Ithamar","He said the goat had been stolen","He offered to resign the priesthood"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:19",verse:"And Aaron said unto Moses, Behold, this day have they offered their sin offering and their burnt offering before the LORD; and such things have befallen me: and if I had eaten the sin offering to day, should it have been accepted in the sight of the LORD?",
   insight:"Aaron appealed to God's acceptance, not to his own feelings. The question that matters is not how we feel, but whether God accepts."},
  {q:"How did Moses receive Aaron's answer?", options:["He was content; he accepted Aaron's reasoning","He rejected it and punished them","He asked the LORD for a sign","He repeated the command in anger"], a:0,
   ref:"Leviticus 10:20",verse:"And when Moses heard that, he was content.",
   insight:"Moses listened and was satisfied. Good leaders can be persuaded; humility receives a sound answer even from a grieving man."}
 ]}
]);
